title: subscribe-daemon never prunes closed clients from state.clients
updated_at: "2026-07-23T08:33:39Z"
---
## Problem
`cleanup_client` sets `client_closed <- true` and clears aliases, but never removes the `client_conn` from `daemon_state.clients`. High IPC churn (`list`, one-shot `register`, health probes) leaves dead records forever.

B278's global list filters `not client_closed`, so **summary counts stay correct**, but the list grows unboundedly (RSS / GC pressure under storming).

## Solution
On cleanup (and optionally periodically), remove closed clients from `state.clients`. Watch races with concurrent accept/`handle_list`.

## Files
- `ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml` (`cleanup_client`, `accept_connections`)

## Related
B278 (list visibility). Found while implementing daemon-global list.